      "answer": "No. The January 2024 inspection report and the March 2024 AD compliance report do not contradict each other.\n\nThe inspection report (completed January 19, 2024) records compliance with FAA AD 2022-03-07 (MCAS v1.7.3 and AOA monitoring) and FAA AD 2020-05-11, and does not address FAA AD 2024-01-02, which was not yet effective at that time (effective February 15, 2024).\n\nThe March 2024 compliance report likewise records compliance with AD 2022-03-07 and AD 2020-05-11, and flags AD 2024-01-02 as non-compliant only in the anticipated sense-the compliance deadline of May 15, 2024 had not yet been reached, and the aircraft remained airworthy under MCAS v1.7.3 until that deadline.\n\nBoth reports are consistent: the aircraft was compliant with the then-applicable ADs, and the later report merely flags the upcoming AD 2024-01-02 requirement for planning purposes.",
